 "comment": "party_monthly paths: with top_n 2, sales shows two parties by name and 'Others (2 parties)' (Cust C and Cust D tie, so name order decides), purchases 'Others (1 party)'; a sub-group party (Cust B); cash or bank, no party (sales and, as ever for expenses, no party with a cash line) and several parties; credit and debit notes in the notes column; a January that nets to nil (no figure); a voucher dated after the period; two vouchers sharing one GUID, counted as two. The Trial Balance: ties within a rupee (direct expenses), is matched by one optional voucher (sales), by the post-dated and cancelled vouchers only together (purchases), and by two sets at once, so by none (indirect expenses, which also carry an opening balance).",
